00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.550
But I want to spend less time on that.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:28.550
Instead, I want to focus our time on talking about how to build the face

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:30.550
recognition portion of the system.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.550
First, let's start by going over some of the terminology used in face

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:36.550
recognition.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:40.550
In the face recognition literature, people often talk about face verification

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.550
and face recognition.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:47.550
This is the face verification problem, which is if you're given an input image

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:53.550
as well as a name or ID of a person, and the job of the system is to verify

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.550
whether or not the input image is that of the claimed person.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:01.550
So sometimes this is also called a one-to-one problem where you just want to

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:03.550
know if the person is the person they claim to be.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:08.550
So the recognition problem is much harder than the verification problem.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:14.550
To see why, let's say you have a verification system that's 99 percent accurate.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:16.550
So 99 percent might not be too bad.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:22.550
But now suppose that K is equal to 100 in a recognition system.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:29.550
If you apply this system to a recognition task, with 100 people in your database,

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:33.550
you now have a hundred times of chance of making a mistake.

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:37.550
And if the chance of making a mistake on each person is just 1 percent.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:43.550
So if you have a database of 100 persons, and if you want an acceptable

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:48.550
recognition error, you might actually need a verification system with maybe

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:54.550
99.9 or even higher accuracy before you can run it on a database of 100 persons

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:58.550
and still have a high chance of getting it correct.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:02.550
In fact, if you have a database of 100 persons, you probably need this to be

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:06.550
even quite a bit higher than 99 percent for that to work well.

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:12.550
But what we'll do in the next few videos is focus on building a face verification

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:16.550
system as a building block, and then if the accuracy is high enough,

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:20.550
then you'll be able to use that in a recognition system as well.

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:26.550
So in the next video, we'll start describing how you can build a face verification system.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:31.550
It turns out one of the reasons that is a difficult problem is you need to solve

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:33.550
a one-shot learning problem.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:36.550
Let's see in the next video what that means.
